                <div class="paper-authors">Qingqian Yang, Hao Wang, Sai Qian Zhang, Jian Li, Yang Hua, Miao Pan, Tao Song, Zhengwei Qi, Haibing Guan</div>
                <p class="paper-abstract">Vision-Language Navigation (VLN) requires large-scale trajectory instruction data from private indoor environments, raising significant privacy concerns. Federated Learning (FL) mitigates this by keeping data on-device, but vanilla FL struggles under VLNs' extreme cross-client heterogeneity. This paper proposes pFedNavi, a structure-aware personalized federated learning framework for VLN.</p>
