To build an analytics dashboard with a responsive card layout that integrates Telerik Reporting REST services using the Angular wrapper, follow this structured approach. The design separates data fetching, report rendering, and UI presentation while maintaining compatibility with Telerik’s Angular integration.

## 1. Component Architecture
Organize your Angular application into these core components:

| Component | Responsibility |
|-----------|----------------|
| `DashboardComponent` | Main container; orchestrates layout and child components. |
| `MetricCardComponent` | Reusable card for displaying KPIs/metrics (responsive). |
| `ReportViewerComponent` | Wrapper for Telerik’s Angular Report Viewer. |
| `DataService` | Central service for fetching data from Telerik REST API and other sources. |
| `ReportService` | Dedicated service for report-specific operations (loading, parameters). |

**Folder structure:**
```
src/app/dashboard/
├── dashboard.component.ts
├── dashboard.component.html
├── dashboard.component.scss
├── metric-card/
│   ├── metric-card.component.ts
│   ├── metric-card.component.html
│   └── metric-card.component.scss
├── report-viewer/
│   ├── report-viewer.component.ts
│   ├── report-viewer.component.html
│   └── report-viewer.component.scss
└── services/
    ├── data.service.ts
    └── report.service.ts
```

## 2. Setting Up Telerik Reporting Integration

### Install Required Packages
```bash
npm install @progress/telerik-angular-report-viewer
npm install @progress/telerik-reporting
```

### Configure the Angular Module
```typescript
// app.module.ts
import { ReportViewerModule } from '@progress/telerik-angular-report-viewer';

@NgModule({
  imports: [
    ReportViewerModule,
    // ... other imports
  ]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

### Create the Report Viewer Component
```typescript
// report-viewer.component.ts
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-report-viewer',
  templateUrl: './report-viewer.component.html'
})
export class ReportViewerComponent {
  @Input() reportSource: any;
  @Input() serviceUrl = 'http://localhost:5000/api/reports'; // Your REST service endpoint
}
```

```html
<!-- report-viewer.component.html -->
<telerik-report-viewer
    [serviceUrl]="serviceUrl"
    [reportSource]="reportSource"
    [viewMode]="'INTERACTIVE'"
    [scaleMode]="'SPECIFIC'"
    [scale]="1.0">
</telerik-report-viewer>
```

## 3. Data Service for REST API Communication

```typescript
// data.service.ts
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class DataService {
  private readonly restServiceBase = 'http://localhost:5000/api/reports';

  constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}

  // Fetch report definition
  getReportDefinition(reportName: string) {
    return this.http.get(`${this.restServiceBase}/reports/${reportName}`);
  }

  // Fetch data for metric cards (custom endpoint)
  getDashboardMetrics() {
    return this.http.get(`${this.restServiceBase}/metrics`);
  }
}
```

