Based on your requirements for a store locator with live inventory data, here's a comprehensive implementation guide using Google Maps Platform. This solution combines **Product Locator** patterns with your existing product API to create a seamless customer experience.

## 📋 Where to Start: Architecture Overview

Your store locator needs to solve three core problems:
1. **Display retail locations** on an interactive map
2. **Pull live inventory data** from your product API
3. **Help customers find products** at nearby stores

**Recommended Architecture:**
```
Frontend (React/Next.js) → Google Maps Platform APIs → Your Backend (Product API + Store DB)
```

**Key Google Maps Platform Products:**
- **Maps JavaScript API** - Interactive map with custom markers
- **Places UI Kit** (Recommended) - Cost-effective place search/details
- **Distance Matrix API** - Calculate travel times to stores
- **Geocoding API** - Convert addresses to coordinates
- **Routes API** - Provide navigation directions

## 🚀 Step-by-Step Implementation Plan

### **Step 1: Set Up Google Maps Platform**
1. **Create a Google Cloud Project** and enable billing
2. **Enable required APIs** in the Cloud Console:
   - [Maps JavaScript API](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/maps-backend.googleapis.com)
   - [Places API](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/places-backend.googleapis.com)
   - [Geocoding API](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/geocoding-backend.googleapis.com)
   - [Distance Matrix API](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/distance-matrix-backend.googleapis.com)
3. **Generate and secure an API key** with HTTP referrer restrictions

### **Step 2: Prepare Store Location Data**
Your store database needs geographic coordinates and Google Place IDs:

```javascript
// Example store data structure
