Based on your requirements for a property listing dashboard in React, here's a comprehensive solution using **HeroUI v3** for UI components and **Google Maps Platform** for map integration.

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

Your dashboard should have:
- **Left sidebar**: Filtering controls (price range, bedrooms, property type, etc.)
- **Main content area**: Grid of property cards
- **Right sidebar/overlay**: Interactive map showing property locations
- **Interaction**: Clicking "Show on map" button pans to property and opens info window

---

## 📦 HeroUI v3 Components for Property Dashboard

### 1. **Property Cards** - Use `Card` Component
```tsx
import { Card, Button, Avatar } from "@heroui/react";
import { MapPin } from "lucide-react";

const PropertyCard = ({ property }) => (
  <Card className="w-full max-w-sm">
    <Card.Header className="gap-3">
      <Avatar
        className="w-16 h-16"
        src={property.image}
        alt={property.title}
      />
      <div className="flex flex-col">
        <Card.Title className="text-lg font-semibold">
          {property.price.toLocaleString('en-US', { 
            style: 'currency', 
            currency: 'USD' 
          })}
        </Card.Title>
        <Card.Description className="text-sm">
          {property.bedrooms} bed • {property.bathrooms} bath • {property.sqft} sqft
        </Card.Description>
      </div>
    </Card.Header>
    <Card.Content>
      <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">{property.address}</p>
      <p className="text-sm mt-2">{property.description}</p>
    </Card.Content>
    <Card.Footer className="flex justify-between">
      <Button variant="ghost" size="sm">View Details</Button>
      <Button 
        variant="primary" 
        size="sm"
        onPress={() => handleShowOnMap(property)}
        startContent={<MapPin size={16} />}
      >
        Show on Map
      </Button>
    </Card.Footer>
  </Card>
);
```

### 2. **Filtering Controls** - Multiple Components

#### **Price Range Slider**
```tsx
import { Slider, Label } from "@heroui/react";

<Slider 
  className="w-full"
  defaultValue={[300000, 1000000]}
  minValue={0}
  maxValue={2000000}
  step={50000}
  formatOptions={{ style: "currency", currency: "USD" }}
>
  <Label>Price Range</Label>
  <Slider.Output />
  <Slider.Track>
    <Slider.Fill />
    <Slider.Thumb index={0} />
    <Slider.Thumb index={1} />
  </Slider.Track>
</Slider>
```

#### **Bedrooms/Bathrooms Select**
```tsx
import { Select, Label, ListBox } from "@heroui/react";

<Select className="w-full" placeholder="Any">
  <Label>Bedrooms</Label>
  <Select.Trigger>
    <Select.Value />
    <Select.Indicator />
  </Select.Trigger>
  <Select.Popover>
    <ListBox>
      <ListBox.Item id="any">Any</ListBox.Item>
      <ListBox.Item id="1">1+</ListBox.Item>
      <ListBox.Item id="2">2+</ListBox.Item>
      <ListBox.Item id="3">3+</ListBox.Item>
      <ListBox.Item id="4">4+</ListBox.Item>
    </ListBox>
  </Select.Popover>
</Select>
```

#### **Property Type Checkboxes**
```tsx
import { CheckboxGroup, Checkbox, Label } from "@heroui/react";

<CheckboxGroup>
  <Label>Property Type</Label>
  <Checkbox value="house">House</Checkbox>
  <Checkbox value="apartment">Apartment</Checkbox>
  <Checkbox value="condo">Condo</Checkbox>
  <Checkbox value="townhouse">Townhouse</Checkbox>
</CheckboxGroup>
```

#### **Search Field**
```tsx
import { SearchField, Label } from "@heroui/react";

<SearchField>
  <Label>Search Address or ZIP</Label>
  <SearchField.Group>
    <SearchField.SearchIcon />
    <SearchField.Input placeholder="Enter location..." />
    <SearchField.ClearButton />
  </SearchField.Group>
</SearchField>
```

### 3. **Layout Components**
- Use `Surface` for filter panel containers
- Use `Tabs` for switching between list and map view
- Use `Separator` for visual dividers
- Use `ScrollShadow` for scrollable property lists

---

## 🗺️ Google Maps Platform Integration

### **Recommended Library: `@visgl/react-google-maps`**
This is the official React wrapper for Google Maps JavaScript API, maintained by Google's visualization team.

### **Installation**
```bash
npm install @visgl/react-google-maps
```

### **Map Component Architecture**

```tsx
import { 
  APIProvider, 
  Map, 
  AdvancedMarker, 
  InfoWindow,
  useAdvancedMarkerRef,
  useMap 
} from '@visgl/react-google-maps';

// 1. Main Dashboard Component
const PropertyDashboard = () => {
  const [selectedProperty, setSelectedProperty] = useState(null);
  const [properties, setProperties] = useState([]);

  return (
    <APIProvider 
      apiKey="YOUR_API_KEY"
      libraries={['marker']}
      internalUsageAttributionIds={['gmp_mcp_codeassist_v0.1_github']}
    >
      <div className="flex h-screen">
        {/* Left: Filters & Property List */}
        <div className="w-1/3 p-4 overflow-y-auto">
          <FilterPanel />
          <PropertyList 
            properties={properties}
            onSelectProperty={setSelectedProperty}
          />
        </div>

        {/* Right: Map */}
        <div className="w-2/3">
          <PropertyMap 
            properties={properties}
            selectedProperty={selectedProperty}
            onMarkerClick={setSelectedProperty}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </APIProvider>
  );
};

// 2. Reusable Map Component
const PropertyMap = ({ properties, selectedProperty, onMarkerClick }) => {
  const map = useMap();

  // Pan to property when selected
  useEffect(() => {
    if (selectedProperty && map) {
      map.panTo(selectedProperty.position);
      map.setZoom(15);
    }
  }, [selectedProperty, map]);

  return (
    <Map
      mapId="YOUR_MAP_ID" // Optional: For cloud-based map styling
      defaultCenter={{ lat: 37.7749, lng: -122.4194 }} // San Francisco
      defaultZoom={10}
      gestureHandling="greedy"
      style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%' }}
    >
      {/* Render markers for all properties */}
      {properties.map(property => (
        <PropertyMarker
          key={property.id}
          property={property}
          isSelected={selectedProperty?.id === property.id}
          onClick={() => onMarkerClick(property)}
        />
      ))}
    </Map>
  );
};

// 3. Interactive Property Marker with InfoWindow
const PropertyMarker = ({ property, isSelected, onClick }) => {
  const [markerRef, marker] = useAdvancedMarkerRef();
  const [infowindowOpen, setInfowindowOpen] = useState(false);

  // Show info window when marker is selected
  useEffect(() => {
    setInfowindowOpen(isSelected);
  }, [isSelected]);

  return (
    <>
      <AdvancedMarker
        ref={markerRef}
        position={property.position}
        onClick={() => {
          onClick();
          setInfowindowOpen(true);
        }}
        title={property.address}
      >
        {/* Custom marker styling */}
        <div className={`
          w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center
          ${isSelected 
            ? 'bg-blue-600 text-white border-2 border-white' 
            : 'bg-white text-gray-800 border-2 border-gray-300'
          }
          shadow-lg transform transition-transform hover:scale-110
        `}>
          <span className="font-bold text-sm">
            {property.priceFormatted.charAt(0)}
          </span>
        </div>
      </AdvancedMarker>

      {/* InfoWindow with property details */}
      {infowindowOpen && (
        <InfoWindow
          anchor={marker}
          onCloseClick={() => setInfowindowOpen(false)}
          maxWidth={300}
        >
          <div className="p-2">
            <h3 className="font-bold text-lg">{property.priceFormatted}</h3>
            <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">{property.address}</p>
            <div className="flex gap-4 mt-2 text-sm">
              <span>🛏️ {property.bedrooms} bd</span>
              <span>🚿 {property.bathrooms} ba</span>
              <span>📐 {property.sqft} sqft</span>
            </div>
            <Button 
              className="mt-3 w-full"
              size="sm"
              variant="primary"
              onPress={() => window.open(property.detailsUrl, '_blank')}
            >
              View Details
            </Button>
          </div>
        </InfoWindow>
      )}
    </>
  );
};
```

### **Connecting Property Cards to Map**

```tsx
// In your PropertyCard component
const PropertyCard = ({ property, onShowOnMap }) => {
  return (
    <Card>
      {/* ... card content ... */}
      <Card.Footer>
        <Button
          onPress={() => onShowOnMap(property)}
          startContent={<MapPin size={16} />}
        >
          Show on Map
        </Button>
      </Card.Footer>
    </Card>
  );
};

// In parent component
const PropertyList = ({ properties, onSelectProperty }) => {
  const handleShowOnMap = (property) => {
    // This triggers the map to pan to the property
    onSelectProperty(property);

    // Optional: Scroll map into view on mobile
    if (window.innerWidth < 768) {
      document.querySelector('.map-container')?.scrollIntoView({ 
        behavior: 'smooth' 
      });
    }
  };

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4">
      {properties.map(property => (
        <PropertyCard
          key={property.id}
          property={property}
          onShowOnMap={handleShowOnMap}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

---

## 💰 Cost-Effective Implementation Tips

1. **Use Essentials SKU**: Most property listing features are covered by Essentials tier
2. **Implement Marker Clustering**: For large datasets, use clustering to reduce marker count
3. **Lazy Load Maps**: Load map only when user interacts with it
4. **Cache Geocoding Results**: Store address→coordinates to reduce API calls
5. **Use Static Maps for Thumbnails**: For property list thumbnails, use Static Maps API (cheaper)

---

## 🔧 Performance Optimization

```tsx
// 1. Memoize expensive components
const PropertyMarker = memo(({ property, isSelected }) => {
  // Component implementation
});

// 2. Implement virtual scrolling for property list
import { Virtuoso } from 'react-virtuoso';

const VirtualPropertyList = ({ properties }) => (
  <Virtuoso
    data={properties}
    itemContent={(index, property) => (
      <PropertyCard property={property} />
    )}
  />
);

// 3. Debounce map interactions
import { debounce } from 'lodash';

const debouncedPanTo = debounce((map, position) => {
  map.panTo(position);
}, 300);
```

---

## 🎨 Suggested Dashboard Layout

